-- title:
--   Upper transfer bound for I^m-torsion of J₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \ge 1$ (a natural number with `NeZero N`), a prime $q$, and an ideal $I$ of the free Hecke algebra `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$, the polynomial algebra over $\mathbb{Z}$ on the set of primes, subject to the single hypothesis that the image of $q$ in `HeckeAlg` lies in $I$. The assertion is the existence of a natural number $C$, independent of $m$, such that for every $m \in \mathbb{N}$ the following inequality of cardinalities holds. On the left stands the number of elements of the $I^m$-torsion submodule of $J_0(N) :=$ `JZero N`, the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $N$ after base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, taken for the `HeckeAlg`-module structure `heckeModuleBar N`, i.e. the one obtained by evaluating the variable at $\ell$ at the Hecke correspondence `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` when these correspondences commute (and by the trivial evaluation sending all variables to $0$ otherwise); here torsion by a set means the elements annihilated by every element of $I^m$. On the right stands the square of the number of elements of the analogous torsion submodule of $\mathbb{T}^L/q^m\mathbb{T}^L$, multiplied by $q^C$, where $\mathbb{T}^L :=$ `heckeLatticeAlgebra N ∅` is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Z}}$ of the integral lattice [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with integral $q$-expansion coefficients) cut out as the image of the weight-two Hecke algebra `heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅` acting by restriction; the module is the quotient of $\mathbb{T}^L$ by the ideal generated by $q^m$, and the torsion is taken with respect to the $m$-th power of the image ideal $I^L$ of $I$ under `heckeEvalForms N 2` (sending the variable at $\ell$ to $U_\ell$ if $\ell \mid N$ and to $T_\ell$ otherwise) followed by the restriction map `latticeRestrictHom N ∅` onto $\mathbb{T}^L$.
--
--   This is the upper half of the finite-level form of rational Eichler–Shimura, to the effect that the homology of $X_0(N)$ is of rank two over the weight-two Hecke algebra: the order of the $I^m$-torsion of the Jacobian is bounded by the square of the order of the corresponding torsion in $\mathbb{T}^L/q^m$, with a defect that is a fixed power of $q$ and with no reducedness, Gorenstein or multiplicity-one hypothesis. It feeds the linear-growth estimate [`ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_inv_linearGrowth_v5`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jZeroNeronTorsionSheaf_inv_linearGrowth_v5), and through it the control of torsion in the Jacobian needed in the modularity part of the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_natCard_torsionBySet_jZero_le_sq_natCard_torsionBySet_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_mul_pow.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeLocal
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeEvalForms
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeModule

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open ModularCurve CuspForm

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000 in

theorem ModularCurve.exists_natCard_torsionBySet_jZero_le_sq_natCard_torsionBySet_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_mul_pow
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime] (I : Ideal HeckeAlg) (hqI : (q : HeckeAlg) ∈ I) :
    ∃ C : ℕ, ∀ m : ℕ,
      Nat.card ↥(letI := heckeModuleBar N;
          Submodule.torsionBySet HeckeAlg (JZero N) (↑(I ^ m) : Set HeckeAlg)) ≤
        Nat.card ↥(Submodule.torsionBySet ↥(heckeLatticeAlgebra N ∅)
            (↥(heckeLatticeAlgebra N ∅) ⧸ Ideal.span {(q : ↥(heckeLatticeAlgebra N ∅)) ^ m})
            (↑((Ideal.map ((latticeRestrictHom N ∅).toRingHom.comp (heckeEvalForms N 2)) I) ^ m) :
              Set ↥(heckeLatticeAlgebra N ∅))) ^ 2 * q ^ C := by sorry
